The tribes of the mainland exist in a far more sparse and scattered state, with far fewer numbers and almost no coordination or connections amongst themselves. Many of them are hunted down by the Houses in the Ashlands or otherwise discriminated against by those who hate and fear them, There are friendly tribes on the mainland who have no qualms about cooperating with the Tribunal Temple's emissaries or humoring outsiders, but many of them are outcast tribes who wander the wilds, and entirely outcast tribes have existed throughout Morrowind's history. One such minor outcast tribe is the mabrigash of Deshaan, which are a gathering of warriors and Wise Women who have been exiled or abandoned their prior tribes. Despite its vast fertile grazelands and defensible highland steppes, very few Ashlanders live in the Telvanni Peninsula.
